<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ubiaja</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ubiaja is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-state">Edo State</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, the headquarters of the Esan South-East local government area. It was one of the Esan chiefdoms whose rulers, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onojie">Enijie</a>, traced their descent to princes and nobles of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Kingdom of Benin</a> and owed allegiance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oba-dynasty">Oba</a> while governing their own lands.</p></div>
